{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789494869,"nonce":"QwnxpEqUe/WYwT2y2xASnu0jS+w=","title":"The frontend has no time module, refuses __future__, and links imports only at the top level","message":"Every speed-center kernel starts with `import time` and half of them with `from __future__ import division, print_function`; nqueens and pidigits import `util, optparse` inside `if __name__ == '__main__':`.\n\nNow: `time.time()` (seconds since the epoch) and `time.perf_counter()` / `monotonic` / `process_time` / `clock` (one monotonic clock) come from the host plugin as `$Host$time` and `$Host$perf_counter` through `zb_time_time` / `zb_time_perf_counter`; `__future__`'s names are accepted and mean nothing; the module linker links imports inside `if`, `for` and `while` bodies as it did inside functions. The speed harness's shims are written in the frontend's subset (no `*args`, no `setattr`, no `str.lstrip`), and the pre-optimisation HIR is dumped to `ZYNTAX_DUMP_HIR_DIR` beside the post-optimisation one.","files":null}]}